# C3: the std submodules mlmf-meta may name. DELIBERATELY EMPTY.
#
# This crate is structure -> structure: it reads a `MetadataSource` and
# returns owned values. It needs `String` and `Vec`, which are prelude
# types and not `std::`-rooted paths, and nothing else. The purity gate
# scans `src/` only, so the corpus differential that DOES touch the
# filesystem lives in mlmf-conformance rather than here.
#
# The file exists rather than being absent because `purity.rs::allowed_std`
# panics when a gated member does not declare a list -- an absent file and
# an empty one would otherwise be indistinguishable, and the absent one
# would look like a crate nobody had considered.
